              "desc": "Rules: 1. Non-zero digits are ALWAYS significant (1-9 all significant). 2. Zero between two significant digits is significant (e.g., 32.50063 has 7 s.f.). 3. Zeros to LEFT of significant figures are NOT significant (e.g., 0.00467 has 3 s.f.). 4. Zeros to RIGHT of significant figure in decimal are significant (e.g., 7.400 has 4 s.f.). 5. In scientific notation all figures other than power of ten are significant.",
              "sciNote": "Rounding Off: 1. Last digit < 5 → drop it. 2. Last digit > 5 → increase by 1. 3. Last digit = 5, retained digit even → drop 5. 4. Last digit = 5, retained digit odd → increase by 1.",
