            "ans": "1. Derivation of v = fλ:\n- Speed v of any moving object is defined as distance covered per unit time: v = d / t.\n- For a periodic wave, when the wave advances by a distance equal to one full wavelength (d = λ), the time elapsed equals one full time period of oscillation (t = T).\n- Substituting these values: v = λ / T.\n- Since frequency f is the reciprocal of the time period (f = 1 / T), we can rewrite:\n  v = (1 / T) * λ => v = f * λ.\n- This is the universal wave equation connecting speed, frequency, and wavelength.\n\n2. Mechanism of Energy Transfer:\n- When a source vibrates, it imparts kinetic and potential energy to the neighboring particles of the medium.\n- Due to elastic forces and intermolecular interactions, these particles oscillate about their fixed mean equilibrium positions and transfer energy to adjacent particles without leaving their home positions.\n- As this disturbance propagates from particle to particle, energy and momentum travel across vast distances, while the particles of the medium merely execute localized to-and-fro vibrations."
